# The directive & workflow stay LOCAL ONLY (per operator decision)
AUDIT_EXECUTION_DIRECTIVE.md
CLOUD_AGENT_WORKFLOW.md

# CLIENT PII PROTECTION (both modes):
# Every per-target business dossier is websites/<site-or-slug>/README.md (emails,
# phones, social handles, owner names, addresses live ONLY there — §11/§11B).
# This scoped rule blocks exactly those dossiers (with_website domain folders AND
# no_website slug folders like websites/acme-plumbing-austin-tx/). The repo ROOT
# README.md and any skills/*/README.md stay tracked and keep updating normally.
# Target folders' other artifacts (audit.md/pdf in with_website mode; Outreach,
# Evidence, data/ in both modes) ARE pushed as progress backup — ONLY after a PII
# scan passes (raw data/*.json captures can still contain page-text phones —
# scrub before push; in no_website mode Outreach channel-target handle line is
# by design per §12B.2, but raw emails never leave the dossier).
websites/*/README.md

# GENERATED LANDING PAGES + THEIR DESIGN SYSTEMS — zip-only, never public
# (directive §3C, §14B.3, §15B). A demo page carries the business's own contact
# details and is an UNSOLICITED build shown to a prospect who has not agreed to
# anything; demo/design-system.md is authored for that same business (§3C.2, step
# N5a). Publishing either would expose the client's details and the studio's pitch
# before delivery. Both are delivered in Deliverables.zip only.
websites/*/demo/

# SESSION CONTACT SHEET — zip-only, never public (directive §3.6, §14B.3, §15B).
# OUTREACH_CONTACTS.md aggregates raw contact PII (emails, phones, social handles)
# for EVERY business in the session — the second designated sensitive file, after the
# per-business dossiers. Delivered in Deliverables.zip only.
OUTREACH_CONTACTS.md

.workbuddy-ai/
